            "heading": "Park ka fawwara",
            "headingHinglish": "Park ka fawwara",
            "body": "Mr. Agarkar apni bhatiji Manjiri ko shaam ki sair ke liye shehar ke bade park mein le gaye. Park ke beech ek fawwara chal raha tha. Paani ki kai dhaarein neeche se upar jaati thin, kuch chhoti, kuch lambi, aur har dhaar oopar jaakar boondon mein bikhar kar wapas hauz mein gir jaati thi.\n\nManjiri dhyan se dekh rahi thi. \"Chacha, jis dhaar ki raftaar zyada hai, wo zyada oopar jaa rahi hai. Wo sabse oonchi wali to kaafi tez nikli hogi!\"\n\n\"Bilkul theek,\" Mr. Agarkar ne kaha. \"Pump jitni tez dhakela, dhaar utni oonchi.\"\n\nManjiri ne kuch socha, phir boli, \"Chacha, ek ajeeb sawal hai. Agar hum pump ko aur tez, aur tez karte jaayein, to kya kisi din dhaar itni tez ho jaayegi ki uski boondein **wapas hi na aayen**? Seedha aasmaan mein chali jaayen?\"\n\nMr. Agarkar hanse. \"Ye to Newton ke zamane ka sawal hai, Manjiri! Aur jawab hai: haan, ek raftaar aisi hoti hai. Par wo kitni hai, ye sunke tumhare hosh ud jaayenge. Chalo, hisaab lagate hain.\"",
