            "explanation": "Given: h = 80 m, Q = 50 m³/s, efficiency = 80 percent. Find: P(bijli) and ek days ki energy. Formula: P(paani) = Q × 1000 × g × h; P(bijli) = 0.80 × P(paani); E = P × t. Substitution: m ÷ t = 50,000 kg/s; P(paani) = 50,000 × 9.8 × 80 = 3.92 × 10⁷ W = 39.2 MW; P(bijli) = 0.80 × 39.2 = 31.36 MW; E = 31.36 MW × 24 h = 752.64 MWh = 752,640 kWh. Answer: P ≈ 31.4 MW and E ≈ 7.5 × 10⁵ kWh approx. (7.5 lakh units). Check: 31,360 kW × 24 = 752,640 kWh ✅."
