            "body": "Ravivaar ki subah Mr. Hirlekar ke ghar akhbaar ka time tha. Unki bhatiji Devyani ne dekha ki Aaji akhbaar ko bilkul haath bhar door pakde hue hain, aur phir bhi aankhein sikod rahi hain. Phir unhone chupchaap apna moti-sa chashma uthaya, pehna, aur akhbaar jhat se paas aa gaya: \"Ab saaf hai!\"\n\nDevyani ko shararat soojhi. Usne Aaji ka chashma pehna aur turant chillayi, \"Chacha! Sab kuch dhundhla aur ghoomta hua lag raha hai! Aaji ko isse saaf kaise dikhta hai?\" Mr. Hirlekar hanse. \"Isliye ki wo chashma Aaji ki aankh ke liye bana hai, tumhari ke liye nahi. Aur abhi ek chashma aur dekhna: Gajanan dada aate hi honge.\"\n\nThodi der mein Mr. Hirlekar ke cousin Gajanan dada aaye. Unke chashme ke shishe ke beech ek **saaf si lakeer** thi: upar ka hissa alag, neeche ka alag. Devyani ne ghoor kar dekha. \"Dada, ye do chashme ek mein kyun? Aur Aaji ko door ka TV bina chashme ke saaf dikhta hai, par akhbaar nahi. Class 9 mein to padha tha ki paas ki cheez na dikhe to hypermetropia hota hai. To kya Aaji ko bhi wahi hai?\"\n\nMr. Hirlekar ne kaha, \"Achha sawal. Jawab 'haan' bhi hai aur 'nahi' bhi. Aaj dekhenge ki Aaji ki aankh ke andar umar ke saath kya badla, Gajanan dada ke shishe mein do power kaise rehti hain, aur do aur cheezein: aankh ka gol na hona, aur lens ka dhundhla ho jaana.\"",
