            "bodyHinglish": "**Galti: \"Magnifying glass screen par badi image banata hai\"**\n\nDemonstration: wahi f = +10 cm wala lens lo (Example 1).\n- Cheez 7 cm par (F₁ ke andar): 1/v = 1/10 − 1/7 = −3/70 cm⁻¹, to **v = −23.3 cm**, m = v ÷ u = (−23.3) ÷ (−7) = **+3.33**. v negative: image **cheez ki hi taraf**, virtual, seedhi. Screen kahin bhi rakho, usse kuch nahi dikhega: rays milti hi nahi.\n- Cheez 15 cm par (F₁ ke bahar): 1/v = 1/10 − 1/15 = 1/30 cm⁻¹, **v = +30 cm**, m = −2. **Real**, ulti aur badi image screen par aa jaati hai. Ye magnifying glass ka kaam nahi, **projector** wali position hai (Class 9, Position 4).\n- Cheez Suraj jaisi bahut door ho: real image F₂ par, chhoti aur bahut chamakdaar: **burning glass**. Wahan kabhi bhi Suraj ki roshni ko haath, kapde ya kaagaz par focus mat karo (Class 9 ki savdhani).\n\n**Sahi:** magnifying glass = cheez F₁ ke **andar**, image **virtual**, aankh se dekhi jaati hai. Real image (screen par) ke liye cheez F₁ ke bahar chahiye."
