            "headingHinglish": "Naye shabd",
            "body": "| Shabd | Matlab (simple bhasha mein) | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Atmospheric refraction** | Roshni ka hawa ki parton se guzarte hue (alag density ki wajah se) mudna | Taare ki roshni zameen tak aate hue thodi mud jaati hai |\n| **Apparent position (dikhne wali jagah)** | Jahan se roshni aati hui lagti hai, yaani aakhri disha ko peeche badhane par jahan cheez dikhti hai. Asli jagah se alag ho sakti hai | Paani mein doobi cheez thodi uthi hui dikhti hai |\n| **Kshitij (horizon)** | Wo line jahan zameen aur aasmaan milte dikhte hain | Mud ke dhalte sooraj ka kinara |\n| **Zenith** | Aasmaan ka sabse oopar ka bindu, seedha sir ke upar | Terrace par seedha khade hokar upar dekho |\n| **Twinkling (jhilmilana)** | Taare ki chamak aur dikhne wali jagah ka tezi se thoda hilte rehna, hawa ke badalne ki wajah se | Raat mein taare jhilmilate dikhte hain |\n| **Point source (bindu srot)** | Itna door ya chhota srot ki wo aankh ko ek bindu jaisa dikhe, aur uski roshni ek hi raaste se aaye | Taara (bahut door hone se) |\n| **Extended source (phaila hua srot)** | Aisa srot jo aasmaan mein ek chhoti disc ki tarah dikhe, jiske alag alag hisson ki roshni alag raaston se aati hai | Grah (jaise Venus ya Jupiter) |\n| **Geometric (seedha) sunrise** | Wo pal jab sirf geometry ke hisaab se, bina hawa ke, sooraj ka kinara kshitij par aata | Almanac mein likha time |\n| **Looming** | Thandi sateh ke upar aksar garam hawa ho to door ki cheez upar uthi hui ya kshitij ke upar dikhna | Thande samudra par door ka jahaz |",
