            "bodyHinglish": "Mr. Lonkar ke ghar mein cousin ki shaadi thi, aur unki bhanji **Dnyanada** shaadi hall ke lawn mein khadi thi. Photographer chilla raha tha, \"Sab cousins ek frame mein aao! Lambe peeche, chhote aage!\" Kuch minute mein pachchis log ek line mein: koi lamba, koi chhota, koi laal kurte mein, koi peeli saree mein, koi chashme wala. Chehre sab alag, par sab ek hi **parivaar**. Photographer ne kaha, \"Ek, do, teen!\" aur flash chamka.\n\nPhoto dekhne ke baad Dnyanada hall ke andar aayi aur ruk gayi. Wahan ek ke baad ek cheez chal rahi thi: uske phone par video call aa rahi thi (mobile signal), hall ki badi screen par live relay chal raha tha (TV signal), DJ ke paas ek chhota radio FM par gaana bajaa raha tha, aur rasoi mein halwai doodh ek **microwave oven** mein garam kar raha tha. Kisi ke beech koi taar nahi, phir bhi sab kaam kar rahe the.\n\n\"Mama,\" Dnyanada ne Mr. Lonkar se poochha, \"ye mobile, TV, radio, microwave aur ye jo tube light ki roshni hai, ye sab alag-alag cheezein hain, na?\" Mr. Lonkar muskuraye, \"Photo mein bhi sab alag the, par sab ek hi parivaar ke the. Yahan bhi wahi baat hai: **ek hi family, alag chehre.** Bas is parivaar ka 'surname' ek hai, aur 'chehra' (wavelength) har sadasya ka alag.\" Dnyanada ne bhaunhein uchkayeen, \"Surname kya, aur chehra kaise alag?\" Is sawaal ka jawab hum Part A se E ke baad \"Wapas shaadi hall mein\" section mein denge."
