            "body": "| Topic | Kya seekha | Ek line |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. Atmospheric Refraction | Taare kyun jhilmilate hain | Hawa ki parton se ray normal ki taraf mudti hai, taara thoda oopar dikhta hai; planet disc hai isliye steady; Earth 15° per ghanta, 0.5° lagbhag 2 minute; kshitij par Sooraj chapta |\n| 2. Scattering | Aasmaan neela, Sooraj laal | Chhote kan 1/λ⁴ ke hisaab se bikherte hain: neela laal se lagbhag 9 guna; violet nahi (teen kaaran); lambi raah se Sooraj laal; badal safed; laal danger signal |\n| 3. Electromagnetic Waves | Ek parivaar, alag wavelength | Sab EM waves vacuum mein c = 3 × 10⁸ m/s; c = f × λ; Radio, Microwave, Infrared, Visible, UV, X-ray, Gamma; Sooraj se roshni lagbhag 500 s; sound EM nahi |\n| 4. Radio, Micro Aur Infrared | Wireless duniya | Antenna lagbhag λ ÷ 2; oven 2.45 GHz (lagbhag 12 cm); radar d = c × t ÷ 2; remote ki infrared; mobile aur Wi-Fi non-ionising |\n| 5. Visible, UV, X-Ray Aur Gamma | Tez aur khatarnak waves | Visible 400 se 700 nm; UVA, UVB, UVC aur ozone layer; X-ray aur gamma ionising; lead apron; ionising aur non-ionising ka farak |\n| 6. Sab Kuch Mila Kar | Chart aur master table | Kab kaun sa tool: c = f × λ, anupaat, 15° per ghanta; pehle unit; wavelength badhe to frequency ghate; laal ki frequency sabse kam; atmosphere Sooraj ko bada nahi karta |\n\nRoshni ke ek rang se shuru hokar saare spectrum tak, tumne ek poora safar tay kiya.\n\n**Aage kya?** Class 10 Physics Chapter 6 Vibrations and Resonance: ek singer ki aawaz kaanch ka glass kaise tod sakti hai, aur sipahi pul par kadam milakar kyun nahi chalte?",
            "bodyHinglish": "| Topic | Kya seekha | Ek line |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. Atmospheric Refraction | Taare kyun jhilmilate hain | Hawa ki parton se ray normal ki taraf mudti hai, taara thoda oopar dikhta hai; planet disc hai isliye steady; Earth 15° per ghanta, 0.5° lagbhag 2 minute; kshitij par Sooraj chapta |\n| 2. Scattering | Aasmaan neela, Sooraj laal | Chhote kan 1/λ⁴ ke hisaab se bikherte hain: neela laal se lagbhag 9 guna; violet nahi (teen kaaran); lambi raah se Sooraj laal; badal safed; laal danger signal |\n| 3. Electromagnetic Waves | Ek parivaar, alag wavelength | Sab EM waves vacuum mein c = 3 × 10⁸ m/s; c = f × λ; Radio, Microwave, Infrared, Visible, UV, X-ray, Gamma; Sooraj se roshni lagbhag 500 s; sound EM nahi |\n| 4. Radio, Micro Aur Infrared | Wireless duniya | Antenna lagbhag λ ÷ 2; oven 2.45 GHz (lagbhag 12 cm); radar d = c × t ÷ 2; remote ki infrared; mobile aur Wi-Fi non-ionising |\n| 5. Visible, UV, X-Ray Aur Gamma | Tez aur khatarnak waves | Visible 400 se 700 nm; UVA, UVB, UVC aur ozone layer; X-ray aur gamma ionising; lead apron; ionising aur non-ionising ka farak |\n| 6. Sab Kuch Mila Kar | Chart aur master table | Kab kaun sa tool: c = f × λ, anupaat, 15° per ghanta; pehle unit; wavelength badhe to frequency ghate; laal ki frequency sabse kam; atmosphere Sooraj ko bada nahi karta |\n\nRoshni ke ek rang se shuru hokar saare spectrum tak, tumne ek poora safar tay kiya.\n\n**Aage kya?** Class 10 Physics Chapter 6 Vibrations and Resonance: ek singer ki aawaz kaanch ka glass kaise tod sakti hai, aur sipahi pul par kadam milakar kyun nahi chalte?"
