            "heading": "Part D: MCB: bina jale band hone wala chowkidaar",
            "headingHinglish": "Part D: MCB: bina jale band hone wala chowkidaar",
            "body": "MCB mein fuse ka jalne wala taar nahi hota. Uski jagah ek **switch jaisa mechanism** hota hai: andar contacts ek **latch** se band rakhe jaate hain, aur ek spring unhe kholne ke liye taiyaar rehti hai. Latch chhoote to spring contacts khol deti hai: MCB **trip** ho jaata hai. Current ek hi raaste se guzarta hai, aur do cheezein latch ko chhudwa sakti hain, **do alag halaat** ke liye:\n\n```\nLive IN ---[ bimetal ]---[ coil ]---( contacts )---> Live OUT\n             :              :             :\n             :              :             :\n             :              :             :\n             v              v             :\n          +----------------------+        :\n          :  LATCH (atka hua)    :--spring+\n          +----------------------+\n\n  bimetal: dheeme overload mein jhukta hai, latch chhodta hai\n  coil: bahut bade current par magnet ban kar latch kheenchti hai\n  latch chhoota, spring ne contacts khole: circuit khula (trip)\n\n```\n\n> **Figure 1.4** – MCB ke andar ka block diagram (sirf function): live current bimetal strip aur coil se hoke contacts tak jaata hai. Dheeme overload par bimetal, bade current par coil latch chhudwa deti hai, aur spring contacts khol deti hai.\n\n1. **Dheeme overload ke liye: bimetal strip.** Do dhaatuein jodkar banayi patti garm hone par jhukti hai (Class 9 mein dekha). Current zyada hua, to patti garm hui, jhuk kar latch ko dhakela. Isme **kuch second se kuch minute** lagte hain, jaise fuse ke table mein (lagbhag).\n2. **Achanak short circuit ke liye: coil (electromagnet).** Bahut bada current coil se guzre, to coil ek magnet ki tarah latch ko turant kheench leti hai: second ke bahut chhote hisse mein (lagbhag). Magnet kaise banta hai: ye Chapter 9 (Electromagnetism) mein aayega, abhi sirf kaam jaano.\n\nDono ke bina kaam nahi chalta: bimetal garm hone mein waqt leta hai, to bade fault ke liye bahut dheema hai; aur magnet chhote overload par chup rehta hai.\n\n**MCB ki rating** 6 A, 10 A, 16 A, 32 A (aur main ke liye 63 A) hoti hai, jo uska lagataar jhelne wala current hai. Uske saath ek **curve** B, C ya D likha hota hai (sirf naam): wo batata hai ki magnet kitne guna current par kaam karna shuru kare (B sabse sensitive, D sabse kam). Ghar ke liye curve electrician chunta hai.\n\n**Reset:** fault door hone par handle wapas ON kar sakte hain. Par agar fault abhi bhi hai, to MCB **dobara trip** ho jaayega: handle ko zabardasti pakadkar rakhna khatarnaak hai. Baar baar trip ho to electrician ko bulao.\n\n**Ghar par adult ke saath (padhna):** apne ghar ke MCB board par bahar se dikhne wale label dekho: 6, 10, 16, 32 jaisi rating aur B ya C. Board ka dhakkan **mat kholo**, kisi MCB ko **mat chhuo**: sirf padho, aur copy mein likho.",
