            "bodyHinglish": "Itwaar ki dopahar Mr. Hardas ke ghar TV par ek purani science-fiction film chal rahi thi. Scene mein ek vaigyanik ek **chamakte hare pathar** ko kaanch ke dibbe mein dekhta hai. Dekhte-dekhte pathar ka rang badalta hai, chamak bujh jaati hai aur wo ek saadharan bhoora pathar ban jaata hai. Vaigyanik chillata hai, \"Tatva badal gaya! Ek pathar doosra ban gaya!\"\n\nBhatiji Urmila ne uchhal kar poochha, \"Chacha, kya sach mein koi tatva doosra tatva ban sakta hai? Ya ye sirf film ka jaadu hai? Aur agar ban sakta hai, to kaise pata chalega ki ban kya raha hai?\"\n\nMr. Hardas ne copy khol li. \"Film ki chamak film ki hai, par tatva ka badalna **sach hai**: radioactivity mein hota hai. Aur pata lagane ka tareeka dekh, bas ek line.\" Unhone likha:\n\nU-238 → Th-234 + He-4\n\n\"Ye ek **hisaab** hai, Urmila. Teeno ke upar-neeche ki ginti dekh. Pehle bata, ye sahi kyun hai?\" Urmila ne ungli se ginti ki aur dheere se boli, \"238 aur 234 + 4... Chacha, ye to barabar hai!\" Mr. Hardas muskuraye, \"Bas, yahi hai aaj ka poora topic: har decay ki equation mein **ginti barabar** rehni chahiye, aur isi se pata chalta hai ki naya nucleus kaun-sa banega.\""
